course: dictionary
lesson: 13365
title: Harvested and what it gathers
level: primary-4
stars: 1
explain: Harvested is a verb, the past tense of harvest. Its main meaning is gathering crops, like wheat or apples, when they are ripe. «The farmers harvested the wheat in August.» The clues are wheat and August, so harvested means picked or gathered at the right time.
explain: The word can also mean collecting other things. «We harvested rainwater in big barrels.» Nobody grows rainwater, so here harvested means gathered and saved. Ask yourself what is being collected, then check your meaning in the sentence.
explain: Harvest is also a noun, a thing rather than an action. «The autumn harvest was huge this year.» It can mean the crops themselves or the time of year when they are gathered.
fact: Harvested means gathered, usually crops such as wheat, apples or potatoes, once they are ripe.
fact: Harvest is the noun: the crops gathered, or the season when this happens.
fact: Harvested can also mean collected, as in «harvested rainwater», «harvested data» or «harvested energy» from the sun.
fact: Hunters and loggers sometimes use harvest to mean killing animals or cutting down trees. It is a grown-up word that sounds gentler than it is, so read the whole sentence to see what really happens.
fact: Context clues such as wheat, barrels or the sun help you work out which meaning of harvested is being used.
exercise: «The farmers harvested the wheat in August.» What does harvested mean? | Left the field to rest | Planted the seeds in spring | Sold the cows at the market | *Gathered the ripe crop
exercise: «We harvested the apples from our tree.» What were the apples like when they were harvested? | Frozen in the snow | *Ripe and ready to pick | Painted bright blue
exercise: «They harvested rainwater in big barrels.» What were they collecting in the barrels? | *Rainwater | Apples | Sand | Bread
test: «The crops were harvested before the storm came.» What does harvested mean here? | Smashed by the storm | *Gathered when ripe | Planted again | Watered slowly
test: Which word is the noun for the crops gathered at the end of summer? | *harvest | harvested | harvesting
exam: «Scientists harvested energy from the sun using new panels.» What does harvested most likely mean here? | Painted | Destroyed | Forgotten | *Collected or captured
